      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SHINES DISCREETLY (4) has come into his own here in his last couple of starts, winning each of them comfortably, including a last-start victory over 2100m. The extra 300m is not an issue, and the hat-trick beckons. HAPPY CLAN (1) is a consistent gelding, with 2 wins in his last 5 starts, each time in the hands of 4kg claiming apprentice Robyn Lynch who retains the ride here. He is again well placed to figure in the finish again. NATIVE CLAN (2) has been holding her form well this prep and welcomes Craig Newitt back to the saddle for this. He has been aboard in 3 of his 5 career wins, and the pair merits healthy respect. JOHNNIE PINCH (3) is another versatile gelding racing as well as he ever has. He was only beaten by a short head at Hobart last time out and will drop a further 2kg for this. Stick with him. OPENSEA (6) has only won once, but that was when Anthony Darmanin was aboard, and he is back in the saddle. Keep safe on the quick backup and keep him safe.",
